{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured /srv/data on persistent LVM/XFS storage, captured a filesystem snapshot, modified the data, rolled it back to the captured state, retained a fresh recovery snapshot, and verified everything after restarting node1.","actions_performed":["Created dedicated loop-backed LVM storage and mounted it persistently at /srv/data.","Captured the quiesced before_change snapshot.","Changed, removed, and added application files to demonstrate rollback.","Merged the snapshot and verified restored paths, permissions, ownership, symlink, file hashes, and contents.","Created the recovery_point snapshot for ongoing recovery.","Restarted node1 once and verified the changed boot identity, storage service, mount, snapshot, and restored data."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Capture an earlier filesystem snapshot","command_ids":["cmd-c2a47b0e5f444436"],"summary":"Shows the baseline tree, hashes, and active before_change LVM snapshot."},{"requirement":"Modify /srv/data after snapshot","command_ids":["cmd-6dc2b67ade6a417a"],"summary":"Shows changed configuration, removed baseline data, new transient paths, and a different digest."},{"requirement":"Restore the exact earlier content","command_ids":["cmd-5937721f32574b12","cmd-e49bda6e5d484bc3","cmd-c2a47b0e5f444436","cmd-b2086b5daea74929"],"summary":"Shows the snapshot merge reaching 100%, successful remount, and matching baseline/restored trees and SHA-256 file hashes."},{"requirement":"Keep restored application data recoverable through snapshots","command_ids":["cmd-1eec889607894af5"],"summary":"Shows the mounted filesystem, restored data, and active recovery_point snapshot."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-0c229354b48e421f","cmd-523f8d4e87b444cf","cmd-9af207a7f1dd4bf6","cmd-1dbaf7dde62345f0"],"summary":"Captures the healthy baseline and boot ID, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID, and recovered service, mount, snapshot, hashes, contents, and absence of